# CLAUDE.md

## What this repo is

`aris-research-workspace` is a multi-idea research workspace template. Every new research idea lives in its own folder under `ideas/<YYYY-MM-DD>_<slug>/` and carries the full lifecycle in subdirectories: idea-discovery → experiment → results → paper → reviews.

## Dependency: the ARIS source repo

This workspace consumes the [Auto-claude-code-research-in-sleep](https://github.com/wanshuiyin/Auto-claude-code-research-in-sleep) (ARIS) repo via symlinks. After cloning this workspace you must:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/wanshuiyin/Auto-claude-code-research-in-sleep.git ~/Desktop/Auto-claude-code-research-in-sleep
export ARIS_REPO=~/Desktop/Auto-claude-code-research-in-sleep
bash scripts/bootstrap.sh
```

`bootstrap.sh` does the following:
1. Renders `.mcp.json` from `.mcp.json.template` via `envsubst`.
2. Copies `CLAUDE.md.template` to `CLAUDE.md` (only if `CLAUDE.md` does not exist).
3. Runs `install_aris.sh` to recreate the `.claude/skills/` symlinks and append the ARIS-managed `<!-- ARIS:BEGIN ... ARIS:END -->` block to `CLAUDE.md`.
4. Reminds you to restart Claude Code so the new MCP config is picked up.

> Note: `CLAUDE.md` itself is gitignored (it carries machine-absolute paths from the ARIS-managed block). Only `CLAUDE.md.template` is tracked. To change the workspace-level Claude Code instructions, edit `CLAUDE.md.template`.

## Creating a new idea

```bash
scripts/new-idea.sh <kebab-slug>
# example: scripts/new-idea.sh joint-delta-statefree
```

The script creates `ideas/<today>_<slug>/{idea,experiment,runs,results,paper,reviews}/` with a starter `MANIFEST.md`.

## Per-idea phase mapping

| Subfolder | ARIS skill families |
|---|---|
| `idea/` | idea-discovery, research-lit, novelty-check, research-refine |
| `experiment/` | experiment-plan, experiment-bridge, run-experiment |
| `runs/` | monitor-experiment, training-check (training outputs; gitignored) |
| `results/` | analyze-results, result-to-claim |
| `paper/` | paper-plan, paper-write, paper-figure, paper-compile |
| `reviews/` | auto-review-loop, paper-claim-audit, rebuttal |

## Path conventions

- `${ARIS_REPO}` — the local clone of the ARIS source repo. Must be exported by the user.
- `${WORKSPACE}` — the root of this repo, equal to `$(pwd)` when run from the workspace root.

## Updating ARIS skills

After `git pull` in the ARIS source repo:

```bash
bash "$ARIS_REPO/tools/install_aris.sh" . --reconcile
```

## Removing ARIS (deletes only the ARIS-managed entries; your own files stay)

```bash
bash "$ARIS_REPO/tools/install_aris.sh" . --uninstall
```
